            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3><span>Picnic at the Estate&nbsp;</span></h3>
<p><span><strong>Date:</strong> Sunday, August 16, 2026&nbsp;</span><br><span><strong>Time: </strong>1 pm to 4 pm (with entry at 1 pm or 1:30 pm, as selected at the time of registration)</span><br><span><strong>Ages:</strong> 18 and up&nbsp;</span><br><span><strong>Cost:</strong> $46.63 per person (taxes included). </span><a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/activity/search?locale=en-US&amp;activity_select_param=2&amp;drop_in=0&amp;activity_keyword=Picnic%20at%20the%20Estate&amp;viewMode=list"><span>Advance registration is required</span></a><span>. The registration deadline is August 13 at 5 pm.</span></p>
<p>You’re invited to experience the charms of a Victorian picnic at Billings Estate National Historic Site. Explore the beautiful grounds and gardens at Ottawa’s oldest wood-frame house. Enjoy the ambiance of a live string duet. Learn the secret language of fans and pose for a photo memento inspired by a carte-de-visite. Guests are encouraged to dress to impress in their 19th century or garden party best! Challenge friends old and new to a traditional parlour or lawn game. Try your hand at plein air art or divine what fate has in store for you with a tasseomancy demonstration. Discover a piece of local history with a short stroll to the Settler’s Cemetery or step inside the museum to see the special exhibition, “<a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/place-listing/billings-estate-national-historic-site#section-fe889061-f82b-40d9-95c4-35af915e772f">Beyond the Brim: Tales Told Through the Hats We Wore</a>.” &nbsp;</p>
<h4>Picnic menu</h4>
<p>Registration includes a boxed lunch and beverages based on Victorian-era picnic menus. Picnic blankets, tables, and chairs are provided. Each lunch is prepared in-house at Billings Estate National Historic Site and includes pickles, cheese, jam, compound butter and charcuterie meats, alongside seasonal fruits and vegetables, fresh-baked bread and a sweet treat. Complement your picnic with a refreshing lemonade or try an old-fashioned raspberry vinegar (alternative beverage options, including coffee and tea, are also offered). &nbsp;</p>
<p>Substitutions (vegan, vegetarian, gluten-free, or dairy-free) must be requested in advance. We are unable to meet last-minute requests at the time of service. While we make reasonable efforts to accommodate allergies and dietary restrictions identified during the registration process, we cannot guarantee a cross-contact free environment.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Notes</h4>
<ul>
<li>The primary language of delivery for this program is English. Any printed materials will be provided in both English and French. &nbsp;</li>
<li>The picnic and activities take place outside on the museum grounds. Check the forecast and dress for weather conditions, including shoes that are appropriate for grassy terrain. In the event of rain, activities will be moved under the shelter of a marquee tent or inside the museum buildings. If the program cannot be delivered due to unsafe weather conditions or other unforeseen circumstances, all registered participants will be contacted directly to notify them of the cancellation and with information regarding their options. &nbsp;</li>
<li>Substitutions (vegan, vegetarian, gluten-free, or dairy-free) must be requested in advance. We are unable to meet last-minute requests at the time of service. While we make reasonable efforts to accommodate allergies and dietary restrictions identified during the registration process, we cannot guarantee a cross-contact free environment. If you have questions about the menu, please contact <a href="mailto:museums@ottawa.ca">museums@ottawa.ca</a>. &nbsp;</li>
<li>The museum grounds include gravel, grassy, uneven terrain. If you have questions regarding accessibility, contact the museum at 613-580-2088 or email <a href="mailto:museums@ottawa.ca">museums@ottawa.ca</a>. <a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/place-listing/billings-estate-national-historic-site#section-fc740f5f-d58b-44aa-a647-439ad640a60f">Additional information regarding accessibility</a> is available on the museum webpage.</li>
</ul></div>
      
