<p><span>Dates: July 9, 16, 23, 30 <strong>and&nbsp;</strong>August 5, 12, 19 and 26</span><br><span>Time: 10:30 am to noon</span><br><span>Ages: 8 to 11</span><br><span>Cost: $7.78 per session</span><br><a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/activity/search?locale=en-US&amp;activity_select_param=2&amp;center_ids=211&amp;activity_keyword=Can%20You%20Dig%20It&amp;viewMode=list"><span><strong>Advance registration is required.</strong></span></a><span> Registration opens May 14 at 9 pm.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p>Learn to dig for artefacts,&nbsp;identify&nbsp;mysterious&nbsp;objects&nbsp;and use techniques that scientists use every day. Inspired by Canada’s first paleontologist, Elkanah Billings, kids will get their hands dirty like Indiana Jones in a simulated excavation site at one of Ottawa's historic homes.&nbsp;</p>
