            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3><span>Tea on the Lawn</span></h3>
<p>Complement your visit to Billings Estate National Historic Site with Tea on the Lawn. Enjoy tea and freshly baked goods alongside our beautiful gardens. Heritage staff are happy to highlight the unique history of the estate, making Tea on the Lawn a memorable addition to your museum experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p>Wednesdays, Thursdays, Fridays and Sundays from<strong>&nbsp;May&nbsp;15,&nbsp;2026&nbsp;to August&nbsp;30,&nbsp;2026</strong>&nbsp;with seatings at 10:30 am, 12:30 pm and 2:30 pm. <strong>Reservations are required.&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p><strong>*</strong><span><strong>Please note that reservations are now full for the 2026 Tea on the Lawn season.&nbsp;</strong></span></p>
<h4><strong>2026 menu and prices</strong></h4>
<p><strong>Three-tier service for one:&nbsp;$21.95&nbsp;</strong>(taxes included)&nbsp;<br>Pot of tea; finger sandwiches; scone with butter and jam; assorted desserts. Admission to the museum for one visitor is included.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Substitute gluten-free options:&nbsp;<strong>$3.49</strong>&nbsp;(taxes included)</li>
<li>Add Devon cream:&nbsp;<strong>$3.49</strong>&nbsp;(taxes included)&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Tea and scone:&nbsp;$6.56 (taxes included)</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li><span>Substitute&nbsp;gluten-free options:&nbsp;<strong>$1.16&nbsp;</strong>(taxes included)</span></li>
<li><span>Add Devon Cream:&nbsp;<strong>$3.49</strong>&nbsp;(taxes included</span></li>
</ul>
<h4>Notes</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Large groups:</strong><span><strong> </strong></span>Reservations of 7 or more guests must be&nbsp;booked directly with&nbsp;the tearoom coordinator (call 613-580-2088 ext. 35258). Groups will be seated at tables&nbsp;of four or six. To keep pathways clear, tables cannot be pushed&nbsp;together&nbsp;and chairs cannot be added to a table.</li>
<li><strong>Allergies&nbsp;and dietary restrictions:</strong>&nbsp;While&nbsp;we make reasonable efforts to accommodate allergies and dietary restrictions&nbsp;identified&nbsp;during the reservation process, we cannot guarantee a cross-contact free environment.&nbsp;<strong>Vegan and gluten-free alternatives are available but must be requested in advance.</strong>&nbsp;We are unable to meet last-minute requests for accommodation at the time of service.&nbsp;If your allergy or dietary needs change, please contact the museum in advance of your seating to update your reservation.</li>
<li><strong>Accessibility:</strong><span> </span>Tea on the Lawn is served outside under an open-sided tent with a stone floor which may be rough or uneven in some areas. A passenger drop-off and pick-up zone is available in front of the lobby entrance. Additional<span> </span><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/node/1007407/" target="_blank">information about accessibility</a><span> </span>can be found on the museum webpage.&nbsp;If you have questions or concerns regarding accessibility, please contact the museum.</li>
<li><strong>Weather:</strong> In the rare event that weather conditions or other unforeseen circumstances&nbsp;necessitate&nbsp;the cancellation of Tea on the Lawn, all guests with a reservation will be contacted directly with further information.&nbsp;</li>
